      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. Higher doses add substantially more risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they don't add much more blood pressure lowering.\n\nYour patient has normal kidney and liver function and no allergies, so nothing in their profile explains the higher dose. Which of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the max standard dose. I can enter it now.\n2. **A different starting dose.** For example, 5 mg PO once daily, titrating to 10 mg. 2.5 mg is typical for frail or elderly patients.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If the dose is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording the rationale. Please confirm it's correct.\n4. **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't controlling their blood pressure, an ACE inhibitor/ARB or a thiazide diuretic is usually the next step. I can enter that order too.\n\nLet me know and I'll place the order."
      }
     ],
